      "id": 1,
      "text": "Benbrook was renamed for James M., a prominent early settler who helped shape the community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/benbrook-tx"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Settlers from Tennessee and other southern states founded the area in 1857, originally calling it Miranda.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/benbrook-tx"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Benbrook Lake, the town’s main water feature, was created in 1952 when the U.S. Army Corps of Engineers built a dam.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benbrook%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Benbrook Historical Society, established in 2012, preserves photographs, documents, and artifacts that tell the town’s story.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.benbrook-tx.gov/187/Benbrook-History"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Benbrook is a suburb of Fort Worth, located just north of the city’s downtown core.",
